# Syncing CyanogenMod 11

## History:
This manifest has CM11 with security patches and bug fixes from 2019 that a fellow dev named Ella merged, but for some reason there were issues with syncing, and this repo has these syncing issues fixed, no need to thank me or anything. :)

## Step 1: Install repo

Run the following commands to install her into your system (repo is a girl, right?):

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.bin
```
```bash
PATH="${HOME}/.bin:${PATH}"
```
```bash
curl https://storage.googleapis.com/git-repo-downloads/repo > ~/.bin/repo
```
```bash
chmod a+rx ~/.bin/repo
```

## Step 2: Use the Custom Manifest

To init(🇬🇧)ialize your local repository using dis manifest, run:

```bash
repo init -u https://github.com/IMYdev/android.git -b cm-11.0 --git-lfs --depth=1
```

## Step 3: Sync the Repo

Now, sync the repo with the following (optimized to the point of skibidi) command:

```bash
repo sync -c --no-clone-bundle --no-tags --optimized-fetch --prune --force-sync -j$(nproc)
```

If you run into any HTTP errors (you will), finish the sync by running:

```bash
repo sync
```

Brought back to life by Ella (tanks a lot, mate!) with <3 and IMY with :miffle_dinger:
